    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP optimizer is heavily weighted toward speed today, making **Corbin Carroll** (85.94) our clear offensive anchor. Facing V\u00e1squez, who struggles with a 4.92 xERA, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill bonus and a 10% boost for hitting in the leadoff spot; he is our premier threat to steal and set the table. **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) follows as our secondary star, capitalizing on a significant 14% platoon edge and a favorable park factor, making him a high-efficiency start in the three-hole. While **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.15) and **Isaac Paredes** (64.57) both provide strong upside against middle-tier arms, **Austin Riley** (57.44) remains a marginal play that warrants concern. Despite his talent, **Austin Riley** is batting eighth and carries a 44% rain risk, which could truncate his plate appearances and dampen his impact in a tight Roto race.\n\nThe bench decision process was tightly contested, with **Zach McKinstry** (38.04) falling just short of the 40-point efficiency floor. While **Zach McKinstry** offered a minor boost due to his ability to exploit the slow delivery of Hancock, his projected ninth-place spot in the order severely cannibalized his value, ultimately forcing him to the pine. Elsewhere, we are monitoring the health of our roster closely; **Trevor Story** remains sidelined on the IL, and we are managing the rest days of depth pieces like **Jose Caballero** and **James Wood**, who currently offer zero utility for today's slate. With **Seiya Suzuki** (51.26) facing the daunting Skubal, we are accepting lower efficiency there to keep our lineups active, but we remain vigilant regarding the rain risk surrounding **Austin Riley** as the day progresses.",
